DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(x^3)^2");
$fun_1 = Formula("cos((sin(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("((2, 7)) U (2, 7)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(-infinity, 10] U (-infinity, 10] U (2, 7) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((2, 7) U (4, 11)))");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("(4, 11) U ((-infinity, 10]) U (4, 11) U ((2, 7) U (-infinity, 10])");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("({0, 1, 3, 5}) U {0, 1, 3, 5} U {0, 1, 3, 5} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({0, 1, 3, 5}) U {0, 1, 3, 5} - ((-infinity, infinity) - [7, infinity)))) U [7, infinity)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("([7, infinity) - [7, infinity))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("[7, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ([7, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [7, infinity)))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [7, infinity))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`0+11-2`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(9.),width=>3}
---

What is the value of [`4*15+10*2`]? [_____]{80}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{0, 1, 3, 5\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \geq 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`(A) \cup A \cup A \cap ((A) \cup A \cap B) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cap (B \cap B) \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 4 < x < 11\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 10\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 2 < x < 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`(C) \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup B \cup C \cap (C \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`A \cup (B) \cup A \cup (C \cup B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 0, 10, -4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -8, -10, -10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 2, -5, -2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<0, 10, -4>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<0, 10, -4>") . Compute("<-8, -10, -10>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<0, 10, -4>") . Compute("<2, -5, -2>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<2, -5, -2>") x Compute("<-8, -10, -10>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-8, -10, -10>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<2, -5, -2>") . Compute("<0, 10, -4>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 5, 1, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 3, 6, -3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 6, -3>") . Compute("<5, 1, 0>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 1, 0>") . Compute("<3, 6, -3>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<3, 6, -3>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 6, -3>") x Compute("<5, 1, 0>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<3, 6, -3>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(0) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>0)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
